   "status": "revise",
   "your_version": "Remember that often the anxiety comes from a childhood guard part of you. It’s what protects you when your inner adult’s Protector isn’t functioning, the same as in childhood. It’s trying to help, making a guess about what’s coming: that you are in danger, or may be shamed, or abandoned, or fail, or be exposed, or be sick, or be rejected, or lose control, or whatever. It can be right! It’s probably been wrong before too, and you know some of those times. Therefore, instead of interrogating that part, start with yourself:",
